[Term]
id: CL:0020050
name: ascending interneuron of myenteric plexus
def: "An interneuron of the myenteric plexus whose axon projects orally (in the ascending direction) along the gut axis. This neuron is immunopositive for choline acetyltransferase (ChAT) and enkephalin (ENK), and forms the excitatory limb of ascending reflex pathways that coordinate peristalsis." [PMID:34170401, PMID:40954253]
