[Term]
id: CL:0020051
name: descending interneuron of myenteric plexus
def: "An interneuron of the myenteric plexus whose axon projects aborally (in the descending direction) along the gut axis. This neuron class encompasses multiple chemically diverse subtypes including serotonergic (5-HT+), nitrergic (NOS1+), and other populations, forming the inhibitory limb of descending reflex pathways." [PMID:34170401, PMID:40954253]
