[Term]
id: CL:0020052
name: stubby Dogiel type I neuron of myenteric plexus
def: "A Dogiel type I neuron of the myenteric plexus characterised by stubby (lamellar) dendrite morphology with broad, flattened dendritic expansions. This neuron is immunopositive for choline acetyltransferase (ChAT) and immunonegative for neuronal nitric oxide synthase (NOS1), corresponding to excitatory motor neurons of the enteric nervous system." [PMID:34170401, PMID:37355216]
