[Term]
id: CL:0020053
name: spiny Dogiel type I neuron of myenteric plexus
def: "A Dogiel type I neuron of the myenteric plexus characterised by spiny (spine-like) dendrite morphology with numerous short projections along the dendrites. This neuron is immunopositive for neuronal nitric oxide synthase (NOS1) and immunonegative for choline acetyltransferase (ChAT), corresponding to inhibitory motor neurons of the enteric nervous system." [PMID:34170401, PMID:37355216]
