[Term]
id: CL:0020069
name: hilar mossy cell
def: "A dentate gyrus neuron with soma in the polymorphic layer (Scharfman & Myers, 2012), capable of glutamate secretion as a neurotransmitter (Scharfman & Bernstein, 2015). Distinguished by a large multipolar soma, thorny excrescences on proximal dendrites, and commissural/associational axon projections terminating in the inner molecular layer of the dentate gyrus (Scharfman & Myers, 2012). In rodents, serves as a major excitatory neuron of the dentate hilus providing feedback excitation to granule cells (Sun et al., 2017)." [PMID:23420672, PMID:26347618, PMID:28451637, PMID:33600026, PMID:34214666]
