[Term]
id: CL:0020074
name: Oriens-Lacunosum Moleculare neuron
def: "A GABAergic interneuron of the hippocampal CA1 region whose horizontally oriented soma is located in the stratum oriens at the stratum oriens–alveus border, with spiny dendrites confined to stratum oriens; the axon ascends vertically to arborize exclusively in stratum lacunosum-moleculare, innervating the apical tufts of pyramidal neurons. Electrophysiologically, these cells display regular-to-adapting spiking with a prominent hyperpolarization-activated cation current (Ih) and theta-frequency resonance. In rodents, canonical markers include somatostatin (Sst) and metabotropic glutamate receptor 1 (Grm1/mGluR1); the alpha-2 nicotinic acetylcholine receptor subunit (Chrna2) is a highly specific marker in mouse." [PMID:10804195, PMID:20421280, PMID:23042082, PMID:29487503, PMID:31420995, PMID:33361464]
subset: human_subset
subset: mouse_subset
