comment: Historically this term was used to refer to all Pvalb expressing GABAergic interneurons, but transcriptomic classification separates out some Pvalb expressing GABAergic interneurons as sibling classes (e.g. Pvalb chandelier).  We follow the transcriptomic classifications. The marker set PVALB, TAC1, MYO5B can identify the Human cell type pvalb GABAergic interneuron in the neocortex with a confidence of 0.691998764 (NS-Forest FBeta value). {xref="https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.11165918"}
