[Term]
id: CL:4047043
name: type 1 submucosal plexus glia
def: "An enteric glial cell that is associated with neuron cell bodies within submucosal ganglia of the gastrointestinal tract. This cell is located in the submucosa, a layer of connective tissue beneath the intestinal mucosa. This cell plays a role in modulating secretomotor neuron activity and contributes to the regulation of digestive fluid secretion and absorption." [DOI:10.3389/fncel.2023.1170309, PMID:28487635, PMID:33731961]
