[Term]
id: CL:4052032
name: granzyme H-associated CD8 T cell
def: "A CD8 T cell characterized by high expression of Granzyme H (GZMH). This cell exhibits a restricted TCR repertoire and elevated expression of cytotoxic, exhaustion, and type I interferon-stimulated gene signatures compared to controls." [PMID:35389781]
comment: This cell type is significantly expanded in systemic lupus erythematosus (SLE) patients. Unlike other CD8 T cell populations, GZMH+ CD8 T cells can comprise up to 50% of all lymphocytes in some SLE patients. {xref="PMID:35389781"}
