property_value: terms:date "2026-03-13T11:13:54Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: CL:4079011
name: lumbar dorsal root ganglion CGRP neuron
def: "A peptidergic nociceptor whose soma is located in the lumbar dorsal root ganglion, characterized by expression of calcitonin gene-related peptide (CGRP, encoded by CALCA). This small- to medium-diameter neuron belongs to the TrkA-positive peptidergic subpopulation and typically co-expresses substance P. It innervates peripheral tissues including skin and viscera, where it mediates neurogenic inflammation and nociceptive signalling through release of CGRP from peripheral terminals during tissue injury (Haberberger et al. 2019, PMID:31293388). In human DRG, CGRP-immunoreactive neurons represent a substantial proportion of nociceptors, comparable to the pattern observed in rodents (Rostock et al. 2018, PMID:29229553)." [10.1016/S0304-3940(00)00772-2, PMID:29229553, PMID:31293388]
subset: human_reference_atlas
subset: human_subset
subset: mouse_subset
synonym: "peptidergic nociceptor" RELATED []
