creation_date: 2010-03-18T03:35:56Z

[Term]
id: GO:0072224
name: metanephric glomerulus development
namespace: biological_process
def: "The progression of the metanephric glomerulus over time from its initial formation until its mature state. The metanephric glomerulus is a capillary tuft which forms a close network with the visceral epithelium (podocytes) and the mesangium to form the filtration barrier and is surrounded by Bowman's capsule in nephrons of the mature vertebrate kidney, or metanephros." [GOC:mah]
synonym: "metanephric glomerular development" EXACT [GOC:mtg_kidney_jan10]
