[Term]
id: UBERON:0001686
name: auditory ossicle bone
def: "One of 3 small bones contained within the middle ear space and serve to transmit sounds from the air to the fluid-filled labyrinth. The absence of the auditory ossicles would constitute a moderate-to-severe hearing loss. The term 'ossicles' literally means 'tiny bones' and commonly refers to the auditory ossicles, though the term may refer to any small bone throughout the body. [WP,unvetted]." [https://github.com/obophenotype/uberon/issues/91, Wikipedia:Auditory_ossicle]
