[Term]
id: UBERON:0002479
name: dorsal lateral geniculate nucleus
def: "The main division of the lateral geniculate body; consists of two magnocellular layers [TA] (strata magnocellularia [TA]) and four parvocellular layers [TA] (strata parvocellularia [TA]) and serves as a processing station in the major pathway from the retina to the cerebral cortex, receiving fibers from the optic tract and giving rise to the geniculocalcarine radiation to the visual cortex in the occipital lobe." [http://www.medilexicon.com/medicaldictionary.php?t=61422]
