name: skeletal muscle organ, vertebrate
def: "A muscle organ that consists of skeletal muscle tissue ensheathed in epimysium, that develops from myotome and that is innervated by some somatic motor neuron. Skeletal muscles are typically attached (via a tendon) to a bone but there are exceptions (e.g. intrinsic tongue muscles)." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7073-9172]
subset: human_reference_atlas
synonym: "skeletal muscle" BROAD []
